-- title:
--   Per-node block for traces of ends, q = 2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and, for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, write $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` of $k_0$.
--
--   **Data.** A prime $q$ together with the hypothesis `hq2` that $q = 2$; a nonzero natural number $M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`); a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$; the hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$) is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the base-changed function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, with the usual compatibilities with constants and with orders of functions; a place $s \in W$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$; elements $\pi_0, \zeta_0, \varpi_t, \xi \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$ (`hπ`); a natural number $\ell$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$ (`hAb`) and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$; a subgroup $H_1$ of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` is the intersection of `levelH q M'` (the kernel of `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`) with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` over $k_0$, an algebra structure of $A_0$ on $K_\ell$ compatible with $k_0$, a nonzero element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$; a maximal ideal $y$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ`, i.e. of the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ of elements integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; a subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ over $A_0$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n$, $m$; $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$; a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal; the hypothesis `hjK` that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC ↥k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K_\ell$; an element $a_0 \in A_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   **Arithmetic hypotheses on the base.** `hqM'`: $q \nmid M'$. `hA`: $A$ lies over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. `hW`: $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value $w$.`evalAt` at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. `hR₀`: for every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of the series modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ`: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, it is Henselian, its residue field is algebraically closed, and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. `hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`, `hζ₀`: $\ell$ is a prime, $\ell \geq 3$, $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \nmid M'$, and $\zeta_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. `hϖtA`, `hϖt`: $\varpi_t \in A$ and $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\cdot u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$. `hKb`, `hϖb`, `hϖb0`: $K_b = \bot$, the maximal ideal of $A_b$ is generated by $\varpi_b$, and $\varpi_b \neq 0$. `htame`: $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$. `hξ`: $\xi$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. `hKℓ`: $K_\ell$ is the base change to $k_0$ of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2 * M') H₁`. `hjℓ`: $j_\ell$ is the coefficientwise image in $K_\ell$ of the $j$-series `jq`. `hϖt'`: $\varpi_t'$ is $\varpi_t$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$, the predicate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) states that $\tau$ realises the slash action by `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`: for all weights $k$ and all modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions, $g$ having nonzero expansion, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent expansion is the quotient of those of $f$ and $g$, and every embedding $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under $\iota$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹`.
--
--   **Hypotheses on the chart point $y$.** `hy`: $y$ is maximal. `hϖy`: $\pi_0 \in y$. `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ (i.e. of `jChartFin`) lies in `ssJSet q Ω`. `hover`: $y$ is the chart point lying over $s$ — for every modular function $g$ of full level $M'$ whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, is regular wherever `jq` is (nonnegative order at every place at which $j$ has nonnegative order), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $g$'s image in the chart algebra and $c$ lies in $y$. `hOrbit`: every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same "lying over $s$" property is carried to $y$ by a level automorphism — there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra and matching $y$ with $y'$.
--
--   **The rigid chart package `hS1`** (a conjunction of clauses, summarised here) requires: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the field of fractions of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$, and $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; the constants of $W_t$ in $k_0$ are exactly $A_0$, the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is generated by $\pi_0$, $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring, $y$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ to the chart algebra, and $W_t$ is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure (`GaloisField q 2`) on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A_0$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose zero locus is the maximal ideal of $W_t$, which is compatible with constants, and which intertwines every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ with the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of the pair consisting of the reduction `redQ q γ` and a scalar $c \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ lying in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the scalar being nontrivial when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$, and the same scalar $c$ being realised, in linked form, by a further level automorphism $\tau'$ attached to some $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ and paired with the identity reduction; $B_t$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is obtained from the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by such an automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and any $b \in B_t$ lying in all those conjugate maximal ideals is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Deck data.** `hn1`, `hnq`: $1 \leq n$ and $n \mid q+1$. `hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`: $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism for $\gamma_0^{-1}$, and $\tau_0$ preserves $W_t$. `hm1`, `hm`: $1 \leq m$ and $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t' w$ for a unit $w$ of $A_0$. `hζc`, `hζcprim`: $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ is a unit for $0 < k < n$. `hjC`, `ha₀y`: `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` lies in the chart algebra and its difference with $a_0$ lies in $y$. `hn`: $n =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the characteristic width of the place $s$.
--
--   **The ends package `hR7`** (a conjunction of clauses, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0^n$ is the identity on $B_t$ while $\tau_0^k$ is not for $0 < k < n$; every level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power $\tau_0^k$, $k < n$; `ends` has $q+1$ elements; level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ permute `ends`, this permutation action is transitive, and $\tau_0$ fixes each end; distinct ends are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K_\ell$, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every end and generating each end as a localisation; any level automorphism carrying an end into $W_t$ already preserves $W_t$; and, for each end $O$: $O \subseteq W_t$, $O$ is local and Noetherian, contains the chart algebra, has constants exactly $A_0$, is residually rational, and admits a crossing presentation — $\pi_0 \in O$ and there are $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over $\widehat{A_0}$ with parameter $\widehat{\pi_0}^{\,m}$, units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ and an $\widehat{A_0}$-automorphism $\theta_0$ of that model, and an inverse $\zeta_c'$ of $\zeta_c$, such that $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$, $\iota$ sends constants to constants, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U U$, $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V V$, $c_y$ lies in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, $\iota$ carries `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` $- a_0$ to $w_V V^e$ with $e \geq 1$, $\theta_0$ computes $\tau_0$ through $\iota$, and $\theta_0(U) \equiv \zeta_c U$, $\theta_0(V) \equiv \zeta_c' V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; together with an Igusa branch $W_x$ (a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ dominating $O$, containing the chart algebra, with constants $A_0$, a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$, carrying a residually transcendental element $t$ and making `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` residually transcendental, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, contracting to $y$, and separating $O$ from the other ends, also after applying level automorphisms); and a subalgebra $B_x$ of $K_\ell$ contained in $B_t \cap O$, of finite type, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, whose elements are regular wherever $j_\ell$ is, which presents $O$ as a localisation, and which contains an element avoiding every valuation subring at which $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental and which fails to contain $O$. A final clause of `hR7` states that every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$, containing the chart algebra and contracting $y$ into its maximal ideal, either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends.
--
--   **Separation hypotheses.** `hR9`: there is $b \in B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and at which $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental (no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$). `hR10`: for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which is not matched with $y$ by any level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, there is $b \in B_t$ which, for every such automorphism $\tau$, lies outside every valuation subring containing the chart algebra and contracting $\tau^{-1}$-translated $y''$ into its maximal ideal.
--
--   **Descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by all level automorphisms attached to elements $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ consists of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by $W_t$ (`hW₀'`); and `nodes` is a finite set of subrings of $K_0$, each of which is, by `hnodes`, the trace on $K_0$ of some end in `ends`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every end $\tilde O \in$ `ends` and every subring $O$ of $K_0$ equal to the preimage of $\tilde O$ under $K_0 \hookrightarrow K_\ell$ (that is, $O = \tilde O \cap K_0$), the following hold.
--
--   First, $O \subseteq W_0'$; and $O$ is a local Noetherian ring such that: for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $O$; and for every $f \in O$ there is $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$, with image in $O$, such that $f - x$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   Second, there exist a natural number $E_0 \geq 1$; a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,w} v$ where $w =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` and $v \in k_0$ is a unit of $A$ (both $v$ and $v^{-1}$ lie in $A$); a proof that $\pi_0$ lies in $O$; elements $c_x, c_y \in O$; a unit $u$ of $O$; a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over $\widehat{A_0}$ with parameter $\widehat{\pi_0}^{\,E_0}$, i.e. $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \widehat{\pi_0}^{\,E_0})$; and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that:
--
--   (i) $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$;
--
--   (ii) $\iota$ sends the image in the completion of any constant $x \in k_0 \cap A$ to the corresponding constant of the crossing model;
--
--   (iii) $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$;
--
--   (iv) $c_y$ lies in $W_0'$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0'$, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0'$, lies outside that maximal ideal;
--
--   (v) the element `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` $- a_0$ of $K_\ell$ lies in $K_0$ and in $O$, and there are $e \geq 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota$ of that element equal to $w_V \cdot V^e$;
--
--   (vi) there exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ such that: $O \subseteq W_x$; for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_x$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; there is $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ whenever it lies in $W_x$, and $c_y$ lies outside it whenever it lies in $W_x$; the dictionary clause holds, namely for every modular function $g$ of full level $M'$ whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and has nonnegative order at every place at which `jq` has nonnegative order, and whose coefficientwise image in $K_\ell$ lies in $K_\ell$, that image lies in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ vanishes, and if that $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image lies in $O$ and, for every constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image and $c$ is not a unit of $O$; and, finally, every node $O' \in$ `nodes` with $O' \neq O$ contains an element not lying in $W_x$;
--
--   (vii) there exists a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ such that: every $f \in B_x$ lies, as an element of $K_\ell$, in $B_0$, and lies in $O$; every $f \in B_x$ has nonnegative order at each place of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ at which $j_\ell$ has nonnegative order; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at the units of $O$, i.e. $f \in O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$; $B_x$ has fraction field $K_0$, i.e. every $f \in K_0$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h \neq 0$; there is a finite set $T \subseteq K_0$ with $B_x$ the subring generated by $T$ together with the images of the elements of $k_0 \cap A$; and there is $b \in B_x$ with the following property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ whose constants are exactly $A$ (for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if its image lies in $V$), with the image of $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, such that the image in $K_0$ of the coefficientwise embedding of `jq` lies in $V$ and is residually transcendental there (no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$ takes a value in the maximal ideal of $V$ at that element), and such that some $f \in O$ lies outside $V$, one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the per-node block of the semistable model of the rigid-level supersingular chart, transported from the ends of the model over $K_\ell$ to their traces on the fixed field $K_0 = K_\ell^G$: each such trace is a local Noetherian ring with crossing presentation $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$, equipped with an Igusa branch and an affine presentation, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ diamond frame at $q = 2$. It feeds the assembly of the descended nodes of the special fibre, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_fixedField_of_rigidChart_ends_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_fixedField_of_rigidChart_ends_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
